@startuml delivery_pipeline_review_phase
title reviewPhase: every review loop in one phase (review-loops spec 1.2.1)

legend top center
A stopped phase halts the workflow: no later phase runs, and the question goes to Keith
with each finding's where, evidence and suggested repair, plus the phase agents' open items.
A loop that ends carried (only low findings open at the cap) does not stop the phase.
A small item is one source file under 200 lines; test files are not counted.
end legend

start
if (Which phase?) then (Design)
  :Reviews: ui-design (when hasUi)\nmaxRounds = 5;
else (Verify)
  if (Build changed exactly one\nnon-test file?) then (yes)
    :Fresh agent counts that file's lines;
  endif
  if (Small item (under 200 lines)?) then (yes)
    :Reviews: code-security (one fresh reviewer\napplying both checklists), then ui (when hasUi)\nmaxRounds = 3;
  else (no)
    :Reviews: code, security, then ui (when hasUi)\nmaxRounds = 5;
  endif
endif
:Every review that applies gets the\nwhole phase change as pending scope;
:pass = 0;
while (A review still has pending scope?) is (yes)
  :pass = pass + 1;
  if (pass > maxRounds?) then (yes)
    :Return stopped:\ncross re-runs did not settle; <<#pink>>
    stop
  endif
  while (More reviews left in this pass, in order?) is (yes)
    if (This review has pending scope?) then (yes)
      :Take its pending scope and clear it\n(the scope carries the pass number and maxRounds);
      :reviewLoop(review, scope)\n(see 02-activity-review-loop);
      if (reviewLoop stopped?) then (yes)
        :Return stopped with that loop's reason\nand the findings that stopped it; <<#pink>>
        stop
      endif
      :Add the files that loop changed to\nevery other review's pending scope;
    endif
  endwhile (end of pass)
endwhile (no)
:Return clean with every review's result\n(carried findings included); <<#palegreen>>
stop
@enduml
